'''Chelsie Marlene Baham''' is the [[Winners (US)|winner]] of ''[[Big Brother 26 (US)]]''.

As a result of losing the Downgrade [[Competitions|competition]] on Night 1, Chelsie started off at a disadvantage and in a vulnerable spot as she became ineligible to win safety in both [[Head of Household]] and [[Power of Veto]] competitions. However, using her social savviness, she was able to build connections with her fellow [[Housemates|houseguests]] that kept her from being nominated. Opting to play a low profile game, she was able to stave off [[nominations]], while also winning an [[Second Chance Challenge|AI Arena competition]] in between when she became [[Tucker Des Lauriers]]' backup target, but her [[Cedric Hodges|key]] [[Brooklyn Rivera|allies]] got evicted instead at the pre-jury stage, which relegated both Chelsie and her surviving ally [[Cam Sullivan-Brown]] to a precarious position coming in the [[The Jury|jury]] stage. There, she formed a crucial game-lasting bond with [[Makensy Manbeck]], which proved to be a decisive factor in Chelsie's survival through finale as both women were [[Quinn Martin|able]] [[T'kor Clottey|to]] [[Leah Peters|evict]] [[Angela Murray|their]] [[Kimo Apaka|ene]][[Rubina Bernabe|mies]] with their combined competition wins. On finale night, Chelsie's confident articulation of her strategic moves, social navigation and overall control of the game ultimately convinced the jury to award her the win, in a unanimous vote of 7-0, over her ally Makensy, making her as the first woman to win a [[Perfect Game]] in ''Big Brother'' history.   

